WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.160
Let’s say you’re trying to
find some solid information

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.620
about a serious health
problem that concerns you,

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.280
like high blood pressure,
or diabetes.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.920
Yet, everywhere you look,

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.640
someone’s trying to sell you
something like vitamins,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.920
yoga mats, blenders, drugs.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.560
Well, breathe a
sigh of relief

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.640
because all we bring
you are the facts.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.200
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.680
Today we look at the effect
yoga may or may not have

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.400
on a wide variety of conditions,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.520
and yes, I do a little myth-
busting in both directions.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.360
The practice of yoga for health
has become popular

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.800
in the United States and worldwide.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.800
A 2016 survey estimated
that 36 million Americans

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.720
may be involved in yoga
to varying degrees.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:52.720
Though the origins of yoga
go back thousands of years,

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.440
it was only introduced in the
United States about a century ago.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.920
What are the risks
and the benefits?

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.800
Yoga users tend to report
having a better health status,

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.880
but that doesn't necessarily
mean yoga was the cause.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.920
For example, yoga practitioners
were more likely to be normal weight

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.000
rather than obese, and that alone
could give you better health.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.040
Of course, if the yoga was
responsible for the weight loss,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.240
then that would certainly
be to yoga's credit,

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.160
but yoga users are also more
likely to be white, female, young,

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.440
and college educated ---

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.320
all of which are independently
associated with better health status.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.040
The same thing with higher
socioeconomic status.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.560
Yoga practitioners also tend

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.720
to exhibit other positive
health behaviors,

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.880
specifically more regular
physical activity in general

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.000
and a vegetarian diet.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:41.880
And the more yoga

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.640
people practiced, the
more likely they were

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.520
to cut out meat, and to eat more
and more fruits and vegetables.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.920
For every additional day
per week of yoga practice,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.520
the odds of being vegetarian
increased 20%.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.760
About 1 in 3 yoga teachers surveyed
in the UK follow a plant-based diet,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.840
much higher than
the general population.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.400
So when you're doing
a study like this,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.920
comparing the cardiovascular
health of yoga practitioners

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.760
to runners, to sedentary individuals,
you can see how difficult it would be

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.880
to tease out the effects of yoga,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:15.080
when significantly more yogis
reported refraining from eating meat

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.960
compared to the other two groups.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:19.800
It's like when I was reading about
the role of yoga in the prevention

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.960
and management of various
cardiovascular diseases.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.080
I was so excited to read

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:27.200
that yoga could significantly
reduce cholesterol levels.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.560
After all, heart disease is
the #1 killer of men and women.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.720
And when I looked up those
studies, I got really excited.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.880
Reversal of coronary
atherosclerosis with yoga?

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.560
I thought the only
lifestyle intervention

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.080
that could reliably do that was
a whole food plant-based diet.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.680
Well, what do you think the
Yoga Lifestyle Intervention was?

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.440
A diet packed so full
of whole plant foods---

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.000
fruits, vegetables, whole
grains, beans and nuts---

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.680
they were getting about
50 grams of fiber a day.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.760
No wonder they got
heart disease reversal.

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:03.240
But what role, if any, did
the yoga itself actually play?

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.600
Now, if yoga gets you
to adopt a better lifestyle---

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.520
stop smoking, eat healthier---
great.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.240
Whatever gets people to
take better care of themselves.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.360
If your tinfoil hat tells you
Martians want you

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.760
to skip the doughnuts,
I'm all in favor.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.360
Whatever it takes.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:22.920
But if we are to tease out
whether practicing yoga

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.920
has any special benefits
in and of itself,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.520
we really need to look
at interventional studies,

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.480
randomized controlled trials
that go beyond just associations

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.760
and correlations and can instead
prove cause-and-effect.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.640
For example, when we find yoga
users have better health status

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.560
and are less likely to be obese,
that could be reverse causation,

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.280
meaning instead of yoga
leading to better health

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.880
and a normal weight,
maybe being in better health,

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.000
not being obese,
is leading to more yoga.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.200
Same with the flipside.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.520
When you read that yoga
practitioners are more likely

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.320
to have mental health conditions
(depression, anxiety),

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.800
musculoskeletal conditions (like
arthritis, gout, lupus, fibromyalgia,

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.960
joint pain, sprains, and asthma),
yeah, maybe yoga

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.040
could be contributing
to some of those conditions

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.480
like muscle sprain.
But for most of these

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.240
it's probably reverse causation:
people with diseases seeking help.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.360
Are they getting it?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.040
The only way to know for sure
is to put it to the test

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:25.880
which we'll explore next.

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.400
Yoga is practiced
by millions of Americans

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.840
and is often recommended
as therapy

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:36.780
for a variety of medical conditions,
but does it work and for what?

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.480
In my last video, I talked about how
yoga practitioners tend to report

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.680
better health status, but they
also tend to be wealthier,

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:47.480
and confounding factors like that
make it hard to draw claims

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.280
about yoga efficacy.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.720
For example, when population
studies have taken factors

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.800
like education or income into account,
the yoga effects often evaporate.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.520
You can't really tell if something
is good or bad

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.360
until you put it to the test.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.040
Unfortunately, only about
a quarter of the published studies

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:08.160
examining the effects yoga on
health or well-being outcomes

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.320
were randomized controlled trials,

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:14.680
and of those, half compared yoga
to basically just doing nothing.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:18.720
In that case if you find benefit,
you don't know if it's the yoga itself

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.280
or whether any kind of exercise
would have achieved

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:26.080
the same or even better effect.
Now look, any kind of physical activity

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.480
is good, but is there more
to yoga than exercise?

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.800
For example, any kind of exercise,
whether low intensity, such as yoga,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:37.520
or high intensity, such as aerobics,
may help with menstrual pain,

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.680
compared to not doing anything.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:44.120
In studies on alcoholics, aerobic
exercise alleviated depression

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.840
and anxiety symptoms
more than yoga,

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.040
presumably just because
of the greater exercise intensity.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.560
Typical yoga is
probably best described

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.920
as a light-intensity physical
activity. For example,

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:01.080
here's the metabolic equivalents
of some typical yoga poses.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:03.760
They average maybe 2 or 3.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:07.720
Compare that to walking at
a typical speed, which is about 3.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.040
So, in general, walking burns
about as many calories as yoga,

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:14.320
and brisk walking would
burn even more.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:18.080
There's all sorts of crazy claims
about how so-called "hot yoga"

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.960
expends up to like
1000 calories, but no,

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.680
you burn about the same
calories at room temperature,

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.480
so 90 minutes would just
be more like 300 calories.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.040
But isn't yoga so much more
than just a workout?

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:36.520
Let's see how the data pan out.
Multiple sclerosis, for example.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.560
We know that exercise can be
beneficial in many health conditions,

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.920
including neurological disorders.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:44.840
And it may not be surprising that
yoga, which involves a series

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.400
of poses, postures, movements,
and breathing patterns

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.400
that could improve balance,
muscle strength, and flexibility,

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.560
should be found
beneficial to patients

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.320
with, say, multiple sclerosis.
Let's see if that's actually true.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.360
No benefit for overall quality of life,
or physical quality of life,

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.840
or psychological quality of life.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:07.520
Also, no benefit for sexual function
or cognitive function,

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.560
and this was all comparing
yoga to doing nothing.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.640
A similar failure to find much
improvement in quality of life

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:16.600
for people living with chronic
diseases in general was noted

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:21.160
with only 1 in 7 trials finding
a clinically significant benefit.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:25.440
Researchers did find yoga
helped fatigue in patients with MS,

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.080
but not any better than
regular exercise.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.960
Same with chronic low back pain.
Yoga might decrease pain

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.000
and improve function compared
to not really doing anything,

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.920
but had the same effect
on pain and disability

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.360
as any other exercise
or physical therapy.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.840
So if you like yoga
and want to make that

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.240
your exercise of choice, great,

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.560
but it doesn't appear to have
any unique benefits for back pain.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.440
Same with insomnia.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:53.200
Yoga works compared to nothing,
but not to physically active controls.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.240
And for cancer patients --
mostly breast cancer patients --

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.720
walking was found to be
more effective than yoga

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.160
at improving sleep.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.640
For markers of systemic inflammation
in breast cancer survivors,

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:08.000
6 months of yoga had a similar effect
as 6 months of non-yoga exercise.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.240
Same with cancer-related fatigue
and quality of life for women

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.480
with breast cancer:
better than nothing,

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:16.520
but no better than other
types of physical activity.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.240
Finally, for breast cancer survivors,

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.520
the effectiveness
of yoga interventions

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.600
in breast cancer-related
lymphedema,

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.600
an abnormal accumulation
of fluid for which

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.600
there's no effective treatment,

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:31.040
and adding yoga
does not seem to help.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.040
There are some conditions
for which yoga really does

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:36.280
appear to pull ahead
of the pack though,

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:39.560
for example, chronic
nonspecific neck pain.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.680
Based on 10 randomized
controlled trials,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.640
not only was yoga
better for neck pain

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:46.840
than control groups in general,
which included doing nothing,

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:51.920
yoga also seemed to beat out active
controls, other types of exercises.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:56.720
The authors tentatively conclude that
yoga can relieve neck pain intensity,

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.440
improve pain-related disability,
increase range of motion,

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:05.120
improve quality of life, and boost
mood among neck pain sufferers.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.120
Finally today,

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:11.280
what happens when real yoga
is compared to sham yoga?

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.920
Yoga is an ancient mind-body
discipline which originated in India

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.600
thousands of years ago,

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:21.320
and that's where most yoga
studies are done to this day.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:24.080
This has raised concerns
that national pride

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.600
might incline Indian researchers
to quietly shelve any negative results

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.760
and just publish studies
showing yoga works.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.720
This fear is not without precedent.

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:38.360
For example, research conducted in
China, Japan, Hong Kong, and Taiwan

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:42.240
was found to be uniformly
favorable to acupuncture;

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:46.560
all trials, without exception,
were positive.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.160
Now, one possible explanation
for this finding

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.320
is that acupuncture is just
more effective in countries

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.920
where it is traditionally practiced,
but it's a little suspicious.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.400
So, are Indian yoga trials
more likely to be positive

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.200
than those from other countries?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.320
They looked at hundreds of
randomized controlled trials of yoga,

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.800
both done in India and
done in other countries,

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:11.840
and trials on yoga conducted in India
had about 25 times the odds

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.800
of reaching positive conclusions
as those conducted elsewhere.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.360
Again, yes, yoga might be more
effective in India than elsewhere,

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:23.080
but it is a little suspicious.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.520
So, for example, if you're interested
in whether yoga is helpful

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.560
for treating headaches,
and you read that yoga

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.280
appears to be helpful
for those suffering from

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:32.120
tension-type headaches,
but then you find out nearly

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.680
all such studies were
conducted in India,

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.880
what do you do
with that information?

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.080
Also, notably, none
of the control groups

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.720
had any sort of exercise component,
though this may be less critical

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:47.480
for tension headaches, since
neither aerobic exercise training...

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.320
nor strength training
appears to help them.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.920
So if we're to believe
the Indian study conclusions,

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.400
yoga may indeed help
with tension headaches,

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.800
but even they found
no effect for migraines.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.720
What may help migraines,
though, is other types of exercise,

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:06.760
specifically aerobic exercise,
decreasing migraine pain intensity,

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.280
frequency, and duration,
at least in the short-term.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.040
What about the benefits
of yoga practice

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.040
compared to physical exercise
in the management

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.760
of type 2 diabetes?

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.280
A significant reduction
in both short-term and

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.560
longer-term blood sugar control
was noted in the yoga groups

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.760
compared to other
exercise control groups.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.960
However, the findings may need
to be interpreted with caution,

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.200
since nearly half of the studies
didn't define and adhere to

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.320
a well-planned exercise regimen
in the control group.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:38.200
Furthermore, an exercise intervention
comparable in intensity to yoga

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.800
was followed only in three
out of the eight studies included.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.840
And, for what it's worth,
the majority of the studies,

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:46.760
6 out of 8, were from India.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.120
When yoga was carefully
compared to sham yoga,

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:53.400
which consisted of chair exercises,
standing exercises,

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.520
and slow walking to match
the yoga session,

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:59.240
the relative yoga
benefits evaporated.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.400
Both yoga and sham yoga

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.360
had identical effects
on blood sugar status.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:08.000
Hence, further well-controlled
randomized trials are required

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.720
prior to drawing conclusions
about the benefits of yoga

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.280
in comparison to physical exercise
in patients with diabetes.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:20.000
Similar tentative conclusions were
reached for yoga for osteoarthritis.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.080
Put all the studies together
and yoga may indeed be effective

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:26.680
for improving pain, function,
and stiffness in individuals

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.520
with osteoarthritis of the knee,
compared not only

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.640
to doing nothing, but compared
to other kinds of exercise.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.440
They had some issues with
the quality of some of the studies,

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.760
and so only a weak recommendation
for the use of yoga for osteoarthritis,

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:43.360
but hey, if you like yoga or if yoga
is the only kind of exercise

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.360
you're willing to do, then
it's probably better than nothing.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.760
Finally, in this video,
let's look at the effects of yoga

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.120
compared to active and inactive
controls meaning like compared

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.160
to other exercise regimens
or just like doing nothing

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.720
on physical function and
health-related quality of life

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.160
in adults aged 60 and older.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.400
Compared to doing nothing,
they found clear evidence

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.360
that yoga improves physical function
and psychological wellbeing

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.440
in older adults, so definitely
better than nothing.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.400
What about compared
to other exercises?

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:18.520
Yoga pulled ahead for lower limb
strength and lower body flexibility,

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.600
but for improving balance,
mobility, and walking speed,

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.560
yoga appeared comparable.

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:26.880
Psychologically, yoga appeared
to beat out other exercises

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.280
for alleviating depression
in older adults,

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:34.160
but not anxiety or perceived
mental health in general.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.400
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.560
about reinventing your health
